# Required browser configuration for email/Google auth, cloud storage and postcode usage.
# Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API: copy the project URL and publishable key.
# These values are public and bundled by Vite. Never use a service-role/secret key here.
# Copy this file to .env.local, fill both values, then restart Vite (or rebuild for deployment).
# Leave blank to use the explicit local demo without an account.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Remaining setup happens in Supabase/provider dashboards, not browser variables:
#
# 1. Auth > Sign In / Providers > Email: enable email sign-in.
#    Auth > Email Templates > Magic Link: include {{ .Token }} to send a login code.
#    For reliable email delivery, configure Custom SMTP with your email provider's
#    SMTP host, port, username, password/API credential, sender email and sender name.
#
# 2. Google Cloud: create a Web OAuth client ID and client secret.
#    Add https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback as its redirect URI.
#    Put the Google client ID/secret in Supabase Auth > Providers > Google.
#    Do not put Google client secrets in this file or a VITE_ variable.
#
# 3. Auth > URL Configuration: set Site URL and allow the exact app root URL.
#    Development: http://localhost:3000/ and/or http://127.0.0.1:3000/
#    Production: https://YOUR_APP_DOMAIN/
#
# 4. Run supabase/sql/schema.sql and deploy wakapoint-gateway.
#    Edge Function secrets: NIPOST_API_KEY and WAKAPOINT_ALLOWED_ORIGINS.
#    Supabase supplies SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to Edge Functions.
#    See supabase/.env.example and supabase/README.md for server/provider setup.
#
# No Gemini/OpenAI key, payment key or map API key is required by this build.
